#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-update-ref(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:7
msgid "git-update-ref - Update the object name stored in a ref safely"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit update-ref [-m <reason>] [--no-deref] -d <ref> [<old-oid>]\n"
"\tgit update-ref [-m <reason>] [--no-deref] [--create-reflog] <ref> "
"<new-oid> [<old-oid>]\n"
"\tgit update-ref [-m <reason>] [--no-deref] --stdin [-z] [--batch-updates]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:20
msgid ""
"Given two arguments, stores the <new-oid> in the <ref>, possibly "
"dereferencing the symbolic refs.  E.g. `git update-ref HEAD <new-oid>` "
"updates the current branch head to the new object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:29
msgid ""
"Given three arguments, stores the <new-oid> in the <ref>, possibly "
"dereferencing the symbolic refs, after verifying that the current value of "
"the <ref> matches <old-oid>.  E.g. `git update-ref refs/heads/master "
"<new-oid> <old-oid>` updates the master branch head to <new-oid> only if its "
"current value is <old-oid>.  You can specify 40 \"0\" or an empty string as "
"<old-oid> to make sure that the ref you are creating does not exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:35
msgid ""
"The final arguments are object names; this command without any options does "
"not support updating a symbolic ref to point to another ref (see "
"linkgit:git-symbolic-ref[1]).  But `git update-ref --stdin` does have the "
"`symref-*` commands so that regular refs and symbolic refs can be committed "
"in the same transaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:38
msgid ""
"If --no-deref is given, <ref> itself is overwritten, rather than the result "
"of following the symbolic pointers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:41
msgid ""
"With `-d`, it deletes the named <ref> after verifying that it still contains "
"<old-oid>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:44
msgid ""
"With `--stdin`, update-ref reads instructions from standard input and "
"performs all modifications together.  Specify commands of the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tupdate SP <ref> SP <new-oid> [SP <old-oid>] LF\n"
"\tcreate SP <ref> SP <new-oid> LF\n"
"\tdelete SP <ref> [SP <old-oid>] LF\n"
"\tverify SP <ref> [SP <old-oid>] LF\n"
"\tsymref-update SP <ref> SP <new-target> [SP (ref SP <old-target> | oid SP "
"<old-oid>)] LF\n"
"\tsymref-create SP <ref> SP <new-target> LF\n"
"\tsymref-delete SP <ref> [SP <old-target>] LF\n"
"\tsymref-verify SP <ref> [SP <old-target>] LF\n"
"\toption SP <opt> LF\n"
"\tstart LF\n"
"\tprepare LF\n"
"\tcommit LF\n"
"\tabort LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:61
msgid ""
"With `--create-reflog`, update-ref will create a reflog for each ref even if "
"one would not ordinarily be created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:67
msgid ""
"With `--batch-updates`, update-ref executes the updates in a batch but "
"allows individual updates to fail due to invalid or incorrect user input, "
"applying only the successful updates. However, system-related errors—such as "
"I/O failures or memory issues—will result in a full failure of all batched "
"updates. Any failed updates will be reported in the following format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\trejected SP (<old-oid> | <old-target>) SP (<new-oid> | <new-target>) SP "
"<rejection-reason> LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:74
msgid ""
"Quote fields containing whitespace as if they were strings in C source code; "
"i.e., surrounded by double-quotes and with backslash escapes.  Use 40 \"0\" "
"characters or the empty string to specify a zero value.  To specify a "
"missing value, omit the value and its preceding SP entirely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Alternatively, use `-z` to specify in NUL-terminated format, without "
"quoting:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tupdate SP <ref> NUL <new-oid> NUL [<old-oid>] NUL\n"
"\tcreate SP <ref> NUL <new-oid> NUL\n"
"\tdelete SP <ref> NUL [<old-oid>] NUL\n"
"\tverify SP <ref> NUL [<old-oid>] NUL\n"
"\tsymref-update SP <ref> NUL <new-target> [NUL (ref NUL <old-target> | oid "
"NUL <old-oid>)] NUL\n"
"\tsymref-create SP <ref> NUL <new-target> NUL\n"
"\tsymref-delete SP <ref> [NUL <old-target>] NUL\n"
"\tsymref-verify SP <ref> [NUL <old-target>] NUL\n"
"\toption SP <opt> NUL\n"
"\tstart NUL\n"
"\tprepare NUL\n"
"\tcommit NUL\n"
"\tabort NUL\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:94
msgid ""
"In this format, use 40 \"0\" to specify a zero value, and use the empty "
"string to specify a missing value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:98
msgid ""
"In either format, values can be specified in any form that Git recognizes as "
"an object name.  Commands in any other format or a repeated <ref> produce an "
"error.  Command meanings are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "update"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:104
msgid ""
"Set <ref> to <new-oid> after verifying <old-oid>, if given.  Specify a zero "
"<new-oid> to ensure the ref does not exist after the update and/or a zero "
"<old-oid> to make sure the ref does not exist before the update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "create"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:108
msgid ""
"Create <ref> with <new-oid> after verifying that it does not exist.  The "
"given <new-oid> may not be zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:112
msgid ""
"Delete <ref> after verifying that it exists with <old-oid>, if given.  If "
"given, <old-oid> may not be zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "symref-update"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Set <ref> to <new-target> after verifying <old-target> or <old-oid>, if "
"given. Specify a zero <old-oid> to ensure that the ref does not exist before "
"the update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "verify"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:121
msgid ""
"Verify <ref> against <old-oid> but do not change it.  If <old-oid> is zero "
"or missing, the ref must not exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "symref-create"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:125
msgid ""
"Create symbolic ref <ref> with <new-target> after verifying that it does not "
"exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "symref-delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:128
msgid "Delete <ref> after verifying that it exists with <old-target>, if given."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "symref-verify"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Verify symbolic <ref> against <old-target> but do not change it.  If "
"<old-target> is missing, the ref must not exist.  Can only be used in "
"`no-deref` mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "option"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:138
msgid ""
"Modify the behavior of the next command naming a <ref>.  The only valid "
"option is `no-deref` to avoid dereferencing a symbolic ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "start"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:144
msgid ""
"Start a transaction. In contrast to a non-transactional session, a "
"transaction will automatically abort if the session ends without an explicit "
"commit. This command may create a new empty transaction when the current one "
"has been committed or aborted already."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "prepare"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Prepare to commit the transaction. This will create lock files for all "
"queued reference updates. If one reference could not be locked, the "
"transaction will be aborted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:153
msgid ""
"Commit all reference updates queued for the transaction, ending the "
"transaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "abort"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:157
msgid ""
"Abort the transaction, releasing all locks if the transaction is in prepared "
"state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:163
msgid ""
"If all <ref>s can be locked with matching <old-oid>s simultaneously, all "
"modifications are performed.  Otherwise, no modifications are performed.  "
"Note that while each individual <ref> is updated or deleted atomically, a "
"concurrent reader may still see a subset of the modifications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "LOGGING UPDATES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:173
msgid ""
"If config parameter \"core.logAllRefUpdates\" is true and the ref is one "
"under \"refs/heads/\", \"refs/remotes/\", \"refs/notes/\", or a pseudoref "
"like HEAD or ORIG_HEAD; or the file \"$GIT_DIR/logs/<ref>\" exists then `git "
"update-ref` will append a line to the log file \"$GIT_DIR/logs/<ref>\" "
"(dereferencing all symbolic refs before creating the log name) describing "
"the change in ref value.  Log lines are formatted as:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "    oldsha1 SP newsha1 SP committer LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:180
msgid ""
"Where \"oldsha1\" is the 40 character hexadecimal value previously stored in "
"<ref>, \"newsha1\" is the 40 character hexadecimal value of <new-oid> and "
"\"committer\" is the committer's name, email address and date in the "
"standard Git committer ident format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:182
msgid "Optionally with -m:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "    oldsha1 SP newsha1 SP committer TAB message LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:187
msgid ""
"Where all fields are as described above and \"message\" is the value "
"supplied to the -m option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:191
msgid ""
"An update will fail (without changing <ref>) if the current user is unable "
"to create a new log file, append to the existing log file or does not have "
"committer information available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:197
msgid ""
"Symbolic refs were initially implemented using symbolic links.  This is now "
"deprecated since not all filesystems support symbolic links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-update-ref.adoc:202
msgid ""
"This command follows *real* symlinks only if they start with \"refs/\": "
"otherwise it will just try to read them and update them as a regular file "
"(i.e. it will allow the filesystem to follow them, but will overwrite such a "
"symlink to somewhere else with a regular filename)."
msgstr ""

